</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduced CogniQ-H, the first framework to apply a soft hierarchical paradigm to the challenging task of end-to-end Automated Data Preparation. By pioneering the use of Hierarchical Reinforcement Learning in this domain, we addressed the exploration inefficiencies of flat RL while avoiding the pitfalls of rigid hierarchies. CogniQ-H achieves this through a synergistic fusion of a probabilistic LLM prior, a supervised LTR score, and an RL value function, allowing it to balance strategic guidance with adaptive, evidence-based learning. Extensive experiments demonstrate that our approach significantly outperforms a wide array of baselines. This work not only provides a state-of-the-art solution for AutoDP but also opens a new research avenue for applying structured RL to complex data science automation, with future possibilities in dynamic pipeline generation and meta-learning.</p>
</div>
</section>
